WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:07.770
You can now access all of the Sequence Read
Archive's vast public and controlled-access

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.200
human datasets in the cloud.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.350
This transforms a laptop into a high performance
computing device and can ease struggles with

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:21.170
speed and storage issues you might encounter
using FTP to download large datasets from

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.109
the NCBI over FTP.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:28.680
This short video demonstrates the steps needed
to access public SRA data on Google Cloud

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.220
Platform, or GCP.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.829
At the end of the video you can link to a
companion video describing access through

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:38.289
Amazon Web Services.

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:42.450
I'll cover these three activities:
1) Setting up a new cloud instance

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.929
2) Downloading and installing the SRA Toolkit
within your instance

00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:51.989
3) Configuring and testing the Toolkit installation.

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:59.640
To set up a new cloud instance, start at cloud.google.com,
and if you are new to GCP, first go to the

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.019
Docs link in the upper right of the page.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:10.350
And if you just want to try out accessing
SRA data, we suggest using the GCP free tier;

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.500
you can read about how that works here.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.590
I've now signed in to my account, and I've
gone the console.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:24.930
To start a new instance, use the Navigation
menu on the upper left to go to Compute Engine,

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:30.450
VM instances, and click Create.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:36.320
I'll give my instance a name, and for GCP,
as long as the Region and Zone begin with

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.020
us-, you'll be fine.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.929
At the bottom of the page, click Create.

00:01:42.929 --> 00:01:45.550
I've now have my instance running.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:51.660
You will typically interact with your instance
via ssh, including for our next steps, downloading

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.509
and installing the SRA Toolkit.

00:01:54.509 --> 00:02:02.860
The steps for downloading the Toolkit are
nicely laid out in our github wiki at ncbi/sra-tools,

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.850
including installing and configuration.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:15.060
I am not going to show the download and install,
but be sure to get the latest version, 2.10.3

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.280
or above.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.069
I've installed that version, and I will show
configuring the toolkit, because there are

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:28.760
a few critical steps required to access these
public data in the cloud.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:34.790
Type vdb-config -i to get an interactive display
for the configuration.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:40.400
The first requirement is to enable remote
access, which should be selected by default.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.680
You can navigate this config menu either by
tab or underlined letter.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.629
Type c, and you can decide whether you want
data cached locally or not, and where you

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.470
want it cached.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:58.519
If local cache is enabled, be sure that you
specify a directory with sufficient disk space.

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:00.870
The next two settings are critical.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:08.870
Type g to set GCP as the cloud provider, then
type r to set report cloud instance identity.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.099
That's it for configuring access.

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:16.580
I'll type s then o to save, and x to exit.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:22.769
If you want to review these steps in more
detail, see section 05 Toolkit Configuration

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.549
on the github wiki page.

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:28.970
Let's run a quick test of our toolkit installation.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.750
Type fasterq-dump and an SRR accession (SRR5368359)

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:41.540
This run takes several seconds to retrieve,
And there are the two fastq files.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.780
That's all for this demo.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.620
We’d love to have your feedback and questions.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:54.900
For help with SRA data and the toolkit, write
to sra@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:02.180
For feedback and other questions, please write
to suggest@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov

